{"name":"Deep Rhubarb","hex":"#7f5153","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"rhubarb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the genus Rheum, especially Rheum rhabarbarum, having large leaves and long green or reddish acidic leafstalks that are edible, in particular when cooked (although the leaves are mildly poisonous).","The leafstalks of common rhubarb or garden rhubarb (usually known as Rheum × hybridum), which are long, fleshy, often pale red, and with a tart taste, used as a food ingredient; they are frequently stewed with sugar and made into jam or used in crumbles, pies, etc."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the colour of rhubarb: either brownish-yellow (the colour of rhubarb rhizomes and roots used for medicinal purposes), or pale red (often the colour of the leafstalks of common rhubarb)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhubarb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rhubarb","blocks":[{"text":"Rhubarb is the fleshy, edible stalks (petioles) of species and hybrids of Rheum in the family Polygonaceae, which are cooked and used for food. The plant is a herbaceous perennial that grows from short, thick rhizomes. Historically, different plants have been called \"rhubarb\" in English. The large, triangular leaves contain high levels of oxalic acid and anthrone glycosides, making them poisonous and therefore inedible. The small flowers are grouped in large compound leafy greenish-white to rose-red inflorescences."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Rheum_rhabarbarum.2006-04-27.uellue.jpg/330px-Rheum_rhabarbarum.2006-04-27.uellue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhubarb","wikidata":"Q7535"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Rheum_rhabarbarum_%28Rabarber%29_Frambozenrood_bloeiwijze.jpg/500px-Rheum_rhabarbarum_%28Rabarber%29_Frambozenrood_bloeiwijze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Rheum_rhabarbarum_%28Rabarber%29_Frambozenrood_bloeiwijze.jpg/1280px-Rheum_rhabarbarum_%28Rabarber%29_Frambozenrood_bloeiwijze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Rheum_rhabarbarum_%28Rabarber%29_Frambozenrood_bloeiwijze.jpg/500px-Rheum_rhabarbarum_%28Rabarber%29_Frambozenrood_bloeiwijze.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young rhubarb flowers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARheum_rhabarbarum_(Rabarber)_Frambozenrood_bloeiwijze.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/CSA-Rhubarb.jpg/500px-CSA-Rhubarb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/CSA-Rhubarb.jpg/1280px-CSA-Rhubarb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/CSA-Rhubarb.jpg/500px-CSA-Rhubarb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bundle of rhubarb","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACSA-Rhubarb.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Rhubarb_Pie.jpg/500px-Rhubarb_Pie.j